// Title: Tamper Windows Defender Remove-MpPreference
// Sigma ID: 07e3cb2c-0608-410d-be4b-1511cb1a0448
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-05 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects attempts to remove Windows Defender configurations using the 'MpPreference' cmdlet
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate PowerShell scripts
// References:
//   - https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/core-infrastructure-and-security/windows-10-controlled-folder-access-event-search/ba-p/2326088
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_remove_mppreference.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "Remove-MpPreference" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-ControlledFolderAccessProtectedFolders " or ProcessCommandLine contains "-AttackSurfaceReductionRules_Ids " or ProcessCommandLine contains "-AttackSurfaceReductionRules_Actions " or ProcessCommandLine contains "-CheckForSignaturesBeforeRunningScan ")
